dax: keep nrpages when replacing entries of another order

A shared fault can replace a real PMD entry with a PTE entry, as when
Fxfs moves a page whose 2 MiB mapping was read before one page was
written. The replacement kept mapping->nrpages unchanged: eviction then
removed the PTE's one page and found the other 511 still counted,
hitting BUG_ON(inode->i_data.nrpages) in clear_inode. Account for the
orders exchanged.

diff --git a/fs/dax.c b/fs/dax.c
--- a/fs/dax.c
+++ b/fs/dax.c
@@ -1070,6 +1070,14 @@ static void *dax_insert_entry(struct xa_state *xas, struct vm_fault *vmf,
 		dax_disassociate_entry(entry, mapping, false);
 		dax_associate_entry(new_entry, mapping, vmf->vma,
 					vmf->address, shared);
+		/*
+		 * A shared fault may replace a real PMD with a PTE. Keep
+		 * nrpages equal to the pages the new entry represents, so
+		 * that eviction does not leave the old order's other pages
+		 * counted after it removes the new entry.
+		 */
+		mapping->nrpages -= 1UL << dax_entry_order(entry);
+		mapping->nrpages += 1UL << dax_entry_order(new_entry);
 
